Package: DEGreports
Title: Consensus Prioritisation of Candidate Genes from Bulk RNA-seq
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Miu Shing", family = "Hung", email = "matthewhungms@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-0412-4374"))
Description: End-to-end bulk RNA-seq analysis that prioritises candidate
    genes by consensus across independent analytical methods. For each
    contrast, every gene receives a multihit score: the number of independent
    analyses in which it is significant (differential expression, GSEA
    leading edge, decoupleR transcription-factor activity, VIPER regulator
    activity, ligand-receptor activity and Cell Surface Protein Atlas
    annotation), ranked separately within up- and down-regulated genes.
    Supports one to three factors, paired samples, interaction contrasts,
    balanced one-vs-rest comparisons and likelihood-ratio tests for time
    courses; raw counts (DESeq2), TPM/FPKM or microarray data (limma), or a
    precomputed DEG table. Sample sex is imputed from expression and used as a
    covariate when estimable. Produces a self-contained multi-page HTML report
    and a script to reproduce each run, through one-command entry points
    (run_deseq2(), run_limma(), run_deg()) or standalone modules.
